module tasks.`2026-11-21-app-memory-reclaim`

task AppMemoryReclaim {
  title "App memory: reclaim parked/closed transcript layouts and cap solved Markdown; drop the PanePreparer's unused 16 MiB icon atlas"
  verify $ cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-term -E 'test(memory) | test(parked) | test(rich)' && make test-boundaries
  paths "crates/bboxy450-term/src", "crates/bboxy450-term/tests", "crates/bboxy450-harness", "crates/bbt-render/src/chrome", "verification"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; one owner per cache; bounded by construction. Source: [[reports/2026-11-21-app-memory-footprint]] (accepted). No true leak (16/16 `leaks` scans zero); unbounded **retention**.

    ## Fix 1: transcript layout retention
    - Owners: harness completed layouts by item `src/frontends/gui/view.rs:3733,3998`, prepared blocks/images `rich.rs:445-447`, model `model.rs:49-59`; term `rich_pane.rs:130-140,380-381` packs view+transcript+rows into `Parked`; `rich_faces.rs:160,195`; `App.rich_drafts` (`main.rs:2294`) has no removal on the closed-retained transition.
    - Do: release heavy Parked state on the authoritative closed_retained edge (keep the live/undo handoff and durable transcript replay); cap solved Markdown layout by bytes for open seats (evict least recently painted, re-solve on scroll; aggregate ceiling 64 MiB across four busy panes).
    - Budget/witness: 12 new-seat churn cycles with expired close grace; in the 192-reply fixture recover >= 75% of added live malloc after grace; broken control (no release) must fail; exact reopen and draft checks unchanged.

    ## Fix 2: PanePreparer icon atlas
    - `crates/bbt-render/src/chrome/icons.rs:163-169`, `chrome/mod.rs:108-119`, `crates/bboxy450-term/src/model.rs:1711,1901`: the worker builds a full ChromeRenderer with a 2048x2048 CPU+GPU icon atlas it never uses. Give it the group-composite path without the atlas. Budget: >= 16 MiB less baseline CPU malloc, no worker icon-atlas GPU allocation; native pane raster and dimming parity unchanged.

    ## Rules
    Reuse your fixture/measure.py/audit.py from `~/mydev/bbx-memory/target/memory-handoff` as the witness (move what tests need into the crate's tests; raw evidence stays out of Git). Long commands detached; one gate machine-wide; harness changes land through harness main then `make bump-harness`. Report with the task's verify command and the before/after curve.

    ## Report from seat:01M80PFYWQ0G27WP2J9A5196ZG

    [[Implement]] Landed the closed-seat reclamation, the 16 MiB per-pane solved-layout cache, and removal of the pane worker’s icon atlas. The 192-reply fixture recovered 82.3% of added live malloc after close grace, compared with 3.7% in the no-release control. Live malloc settled at 56.6 MiB after twelve more expired seats. The worker’s 16,793,600-byte icon-atlas stack disappeared. The assigned verification, native rendering checks, and both landing gates exited 0. The terminal gate checked 991 native/TLC model results, including the failing no-release control.

    ```json
